  ok   an unattended start whose facts could not be read gets no pack
  ok   a person's terminal still gets the degraded pack, which says what it could not read
  ok   an unattended start with every required source answered compiles as before
  ok   what a session must carry is decided by the trigger the LAUNCH passes, not guessed from the journal
  ok   the project source counts as met only when the project row EXISTS
  ok   facts past one read are COUNTED: omittedFacts includes what the gateway did not return
  ok   the budget includes oversized project/task input and rejects instead of truncating authority
  ok   invalid and impossibly small budgets cannot produce a pack
  ok   facts, sessions, warning, omission footer and final newline share one exact UTF-16 budget
  ok   an empty pack fits its exact size, including the final newline

all green: an unattended start runs on its required context or not at all
